.TH "NIAC" "1" "Sep 2026" "NIAC" "NIAC Manual"

.SH NAME
niac-content-install - Install a content bundle into the library


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac content install [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Install a versioned content bundle (gzip-tar) into the local library
from a local file — no network access is made.

.PP
The bundle's top-level directories must be one of: networks, walks,
pcaps. Anything else is rejected. Each entry is re-rooted under
// before any file is touched, so a malicious bundle
cannot escape the library.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--bundle\fP=""
	Local bundle file to install (required)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print what would be installed without writing files

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	Overwrite your own files and any bundle file you have edited (default: preserve them)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for install

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	Library root (default: NIAC_LIBRARY_ROOT or ~/.niac/library)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Install from a local bundle
  niac content install --bundle ./niac-content-v0.66.41.tar.gz

  # Install into a custom root
  niac content install --bundle ./niac-content.tar.gz --root /var/lib/niac/library

  # Preview what would be installed
  niac content install --bundle ./niac-content.tar.gz --dry-run
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-content(1)\fP


